[TEXT] Found it immediately. On **router_core_3**, the FORWARD chain has a blanket DROP rule hitting all traffic destined for `10.200.0.0/24`:

```
FORWARD rule 1: DROP  proto all  src 0.0.0.0/0  dst 10.200.0.0/24   (12 pkts / 1008 bytes)
```

This was added during the "firewall change window". The routing plane is completely healthy (OSPF routes correct on all routers, switch_server_access has back-routes to both pod subnets), but every forwarded packet from either pod heading toward any server gets silently dropped at router_core_3 before it can be forwarded onto eth2/switch_server_access. The counter of 12 packets confirms active drops. switch_server_access itself has no firewall rules. Everything within the server farm works because that traffic never crosses router_core_3's FORWARD chain.

